# Product Goal (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/foundation/product-goal.md`.

**Intent.** SR-App runs the daily operations of a snowmobile field service company from one
internal tool. North star: **a field agent can go from "assigned a job" to "job done + invoice +
payment recorded" on a phone, in the field, tolerant of bad signal**, while dispatch watches it happen.

**Users (exactly three):** `FIELD_AGENT` (mobile technician), `DISPATCH` (admin/back-office),
`OWNER` (admin + oversight + user management).

**Hard rules**
- Every feature must serve at least one of the three users; state which one and which workflow it advances.
- **Field speed wins** over admin richness when they conflict on the mobile surface.
- The **Job** is the operational system of record; everything hangs off jobs.
- Truthfulness over impressiveness — never present a capability that isn't really delivered.

**Failure modes:** admin richness that slows the field surface; features with no clear user among
the three; drifting toward a generic CRM.

**Escalation:** if a feature doesn't clearly serve one of the three users or conflicts with the
north star, stop and log a decision (`docs/decision-log.md`).
